{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
I've [Em]got a mule, her [B7]name is [Em]Sal,
[Am]Fifteen miles on the [Em]Erie [B7]Ca[Em]nal,
She's a [Em]good old worker and a [B7]good old [Em]pal,
[Am]Fifteen miles on the [Em]Erie [B7]Ca[Em]nal.
We've [Em]haul'd some barges [Am]in our [Em]day,
[Em]Fill'd with lumber, [Am]coal and [Em]hay,
And we [Em]know ev'ry inch [Am]of the [Em]way
From [Em]Albany [B7]to Buffa[Em]lo.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Low bridge, ev'ry[D]body down!
[D7]Low bridge, for we're [G]going through a town,
And you'll [C]always know your [G]neighbor,
You'll [C]always know your [G]pal,
If you [Em]ever navigated
[B7]On the Erie Ca[Em]nal.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
We [Em]better get along on our [B7]way, old [Em]gal,
[Am]Fifteen miles on the [Em]Erie [B7]Ca[Em]nal,
'Cause you [Em]bet your life I'd [B7]never part with [Em]Sal
[Am]Fifteen miles on the [Em]Erie [B7]Ca[Em]nal.
Git [Em]up there, mule, [Am]here comes a [Em]lock,
[Em]We'll make Rome 'bout [Am]six o'[Em]clock,
[Em]One more trip and [Am]back we'll [Em]go,
Right [Em]back home [B7]to Buffa[Em]lo.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: Em}
